---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

// V-690 — Sessions API developer docs. Sibling to api-quickstart;
// this is the deeper "every field, every lifecycle event" reference
// for the /v1/sessions surface.

const LIFECYCLE = [
  { state: 'creating', desc: 'Backend received the start request; provisioning a browser instance.' },
  { state: 'ready', desc: 'Browser ready; the session URL is reachable.' },
  { state: 'busy', desc: 'Session is actively running an automation step.' },
  { state: 'destroyed', desc: 'Normal end-of-life; recording (if any) is finalised.' },
  { state: 'errored', desc: 'Abnormal termination; check the error field for details.' },
];
---

<BaseLayout title="Sessions API — Driftstack developer docs" description="Start, monitor, end browser sessions. Lifecycle, fields, recordings.">
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-12 prose prose-slate dark:prose-invert">
    <h1>Sessions</h1>

    <p class="lead">
      A session is one running browser instance Driftstack manages
      for you. This page is the reference for the
      <code>/v1/sessions</code> surface; for the 60-second walkthrough
      see <a href="/docs/api-quickstart">api-quickstart</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Lifecycle</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>State</th><th>What it means</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {LIFECYCLE.map((s) => (
          <tr><td><code>{s.state}</code></td><td>{s.desc}</td></tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      Transitions: <code>creating → ready → busy → destroyed</code>
      is the happy path. <code>errored</code> is terminal; the
      session cannot recover.
    </p>

    <h2>POST /v1/sessions</h2>
    <pre><code>{`POST /v1/sessions
Authorization: Bearer ds_live_…
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "target_url": "https://example.com",
  "profile_archetype": "default",
  "profile_id": "prof_…",                ← optional, pin to a saved profile
  "record": true,                         ← optional, default false
  "metadata": { "ticket": "JIRA-1234" }   ← optional, surfaced in webhooks
}

→ 201 Created
{
  "session": {
    "id": "sess_…",
    "status": "creating",
    "live_url": "https://app.driftstack.dev/sessions/sess_…",
    "created_at": "2026-05-11T12:00:00.000Z"
  }
}`}</code></pre>
    <p>
      The session moves to <code>ready</code> within ~10 seconds
      (the driver bootstrap time). Poll <code>GET /v1/sessions/:id</code>
      or subscribe to the <code>session.completed</code> /
      <code>session.failed</code> webhooks for status changes.
    </p>

    <h2>GET /v1/sessions/:id</h2>
    <pre><code>{`GET /v1/sessions/sess_…
Authorization: Bearer ds_live_…

→ 200 OK
{
  "session": {
    "id": "sess_…",
    "status": "running",
    "target_url": "https://example.com",
    "profile_archetype": "default",
    "live_url": "https://app.driftstack.dev/sessions/sess_…",
    "created_at": "2026-05-11T12:00:00.000Z",
    "ready_at": "2026-05-11T12:00:08.000Z",
    "ended_at": null,
    "error": null,
    "metadata": { "ticket": "JIRA-1234" }
  }
}`}</code></pre>

    <h2>GET /v1/sessions — list</h2>
    <pre><code>{`GET /v1/sessions?limit=25&status=ready
Authorization: Bearer ds_live_…

→ 200 OK
{
  "sessions": [...],
  "nextCursor": "cur_…"   ← null when no more pages
}`}</code></pre>
    <p>
      Cursor pagination. Pass the previous response's
      <code>nextCursor</code> as <code>?cursor=</code> on the next
      request. Default page size 25; max 100. Filter by
      <code>status</code> if you only want a subset (e.g.
      <code>?status=errored</code> for failure auditing).
    </p>

    <h2>DELETE /v1/sessions/:id</h2>
    <pre><code>{`DELETE /v1/sessions/sess_…
Authorization: Bearer ds_live_…

→ 204 No Content`}</code></pre>
    <p>
      Ends the session immediately. Recording is finalised; the
      session moves to <code>destroyed</code>. Idempotent —
      <code>DELETE</code>ing an already-destroyed session also
      returns 204.
    </p>

    <h2>GET /v1/sessions/:id/recording</h2>
    <p>
      When the session was started with <code>record: true</code>,
      a video recording is stored after the session ends. Fetch it:
    </p>
    <pre><code>{`GET /v1/sessions/sess_…/recording
Authorization: Bearer ds_live_…

→ 200 OK
{
  "playback_url": "https://r2-…/recordings/…?sig=…",
  "expires_at": "2026-05-11T13:00:00.000Z"
}`}</code></pre>
    <p>
      The URL is presigned and expires in 1 hour. Refresh by calling
      the endpoint again. Recordings are kept for 30 days by default
      (90 days on API Builder + above).
    </p>

    <h2>Concurrent session limits</h2>
    <p>
      Each tier caps the number of sessions you can have in
      <code>creating</code> + <code>ready</code> + <code>busy</code>
      states at once. See <a href="/docs/rate-limits">rate-limits</a>
      for the per-tier table. Hitting the cap returns 409 Conflict
      (not 429); wait for an existing session to finish or upgrade
      your tier.
    </p>

    <h2>Webhooks</h2>
    <p>
      Subscribe to <code>session.completed</code> +
      <code>session.failed</code> (and optionally
      <code>session.recording_ready</code>) instead of polling. See
      <a href="/docs/webhooks">/docs/webhooks</a> for the delivery
      format + signature verification.
    </p>

    <h2>Profile archetypes</h2>
    <p>
      The <code>profile_archetype</code> parameter selects the
      user-agent + viewport + locale preset to apply. Built-in
      values:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><code>default</code> — anonymous Chrome on Linux.</li>
      <li><code>mobile_ios</code> — Safari on iOS.</li>
      <li><code>mobile_android</code> — Chrome on Android.</li>
      <li><code>kiosk</code> — full-screen, no chrome.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      For consistent identity across runs (e.g. logged-in scraping),
      mint a saved profile via <code>POST /v1/profiles</code> and
      pass its <code>profile_id</code> instead.
    </p>

    <h2>Support</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="mailto:developers@driftstack.dev">developers@driftstack.dev</a>.
    </p>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
